        ('Fluid Properties', 'At the same elevation in a continuous static liquid, pressure is:', 'Different at every point', 'The same', 'Always atmospheric', 'Zero gauge in all cases', 'B', 'Hydrostatic pressure is equal along a horizontal plane in a connected fluid at rest.', 'easy', 14),
        ('Fluid Properties', 'Pascal law states that an applied pressure change to a confined fluid is:', 'Transmitted undiminished throughout the fluid', 'Lost completely at the boundary', 'Converted only into velocity', 'Independent of the fluid', 'A', 'A pressure change applied to a confined fluid is transmitted throughout it.', 'easy', 15),
        ('Fluid Properties', 'The resultant hydrostatic force on a plane surface is based on pressure at the:', 'Centroid multiplied by area', 'Top edge multiplied by perimeter', 'Bottom edge divided by area', 'Center of pressure multiplied by depth', 'A', 'For a plane surface, resultant force equals pressure at the centroid times area.', 'medium', 16),
        ('Fluid Properties', 'For a vertical submerged plane surface, the center of pressure is normally:', 'Above the centroid', 'At the free surface', 'Below the centroid', 'Independent of depth', 'C', 'Pressure increases with depth, shifting the resultant below the centroid.', 'medium', 17),
        ('Fluid Properties', 'Buoyant force on a submerged body equals the weight of:', 'The body material only', 'The displaced fluid', 'Fluid above the body only', 'The surrounding container', 'B', 'Archimedes principle equates buoyancy to the weight of displaced fluid.', 'easy', 18),
        ('Fluid Properties', 'A floating body is in stable equilibrium for small angular displacement when its metacenter is:', 'Below its center of gravity', 'Above its center of gravity', 'At the bottom of the body', 'At the center of buoyancy in every case', 'B', 'Positive metacentric height, with metacenter above the center of gravity, gives initial stability.', 'medium', 19),
